.TH DEXY 1 "June 2026" "dexy 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dexy \- keep your Mac wide awake; lid closed, on battery, no nonsense
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dexy
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dexy
is a one-word toggle for macOS's "never sleep \(em even with the lid shut" mode.
It is a thin wrapper around
.BR pmset (1)'s
.B SleepDisabled
power-management flag, which is the real switch behind keeping a MacBook awake
while the lid is closed and running on battery.
.PP
With no command,
.B dexy
toggles the state. Turning the state on or off is a privileged operation, so
.BR on ,
.BR off ,
and the bare toggle run
.BR pmset (1)
under
.BR sudo (8)
and may prompt for your password.
.B status
never needs sudo.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (none)
Toggle dexy on or off.
.TP
.B on
Stay awake \(em disable sleep, even with the lid shut.
.TP
.B off
Restore normal sleep. Battery idle-sleep is put back to whatever it was when
.B dexy
was turned on (remembered in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/dexy/battery-sleep ),
or to
.B DEXY_SLEEP_MINUTES
if that is set, or 5 minutes as a last resort.
.TP
.B status
Show the current state without changing it.
.TP
.B setup-sudo
Allow passwordless toggling. Installs a
.BR sudoers (5)
drop-in at
.I /etc/sudoers.d/dexy
that lets you run only the exact
.BR pmset (1)
commands dexy uses \(em without a password. The rule is validated with
.BR visudo (8)
before installation, which asks for your password once to write the file.
Optional; without it, dexy simply prompts on each toggle.
.TP
.B remove-sudo
Remove the drop-in installed by
.BR "dexy setup-sudo" .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Show the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEXY_SLEEP_MINUTES
Override the battery idle-sleep timeout that
.B "dexy off"
restores. When unset,
.B dexy
restores the value it remembered when turned on (falling back to 5 minutes).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables coloured output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/dexy/battery-sleep
Battery idle-sleep timeout remembered when
.B dexy
was turned on, so
.B "dexy off"
can restore it.
.RB ( $XDG_STATE_HOME
defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state .)
This is the only state dexy keeps.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/dexy
Optional sudoers drop-in created by
.B "dexy setup-sudo"
and removed by
.BR "dexy remove-sudo" .
Grants passwordless
.BR sudo (8)
for only the
.BR pmset (1)
commands dexy runs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Stay awake before closing the lid for a long build:
.B dexy on
.TP
Check whether you left it on:
.B dexy status
.TP
Go back to normal, restoring a 10-minute sleep:
.B DEXY_SLEEP_MINUTES=10 dexy off
.TP
Stop being asked for your password on every toggle:
.B dexy setup-sudo
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmset (1),
.BR caffeinate (8),
.BR sudoers (5),
.BR visudo (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Jonathan O'Brien.
Source and issues:
